# Copy to .env (gitignored) and run with `uv run --env-file .env app.py ...`. Variables already set in the
# environment win. The test suite never reads this file and never calls a model.

# Where requests go: none (print the request), anthropic or openai.
DOCS_QA_PROVIDER=anthropic

# Who is signed in: u_ada (default), u_ben or u_cho, from data/accounts.json.
# DOCS_QA_USER=u_ada

# Each route names its model per provider in policy/routes.json: claude-haiku-4-5 and claude-opus-5-5 for anthropic;
# for openai, a local gpt-oss-20b on the small route and gpt-oss-120b on Groq on the large one. DOCS_QA_MODEL sends the
# chosen route to another model on the same endpoint.
# DOCS_QA_MODEL=

# The Claude API. Or leave the key unset after `ant auth login`.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# OpenAI, or any OpenAI-compatible server (Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM, llama.cpp) through OPENAI_BASE_URL.
# DOCS_QA_PROVIDER=openai
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# The large route's openai endpoint, Groq, reads its key from here (api_key_env in policy/routes.json).
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
